---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---
<SiteLayout title="About InfiniCharm" description="Learn about the InfiniCharm project and its staged development plan.">
  <section class="page-hero container about-hero"><p class="eyebrow">A TECHILY FLY PROJECT</p><h1>Start simple.<br /><span class="coral-text">Build with care.</span></h1><p class="page-intro">InfiniCharm is being built as a multi-vendor marketplace across web, mobile, and desktop. We are starting with a reliable web foundation before connecting the backend and cross-platform apps.</p></section>
  <section class="container section roadmap-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">THE BUILD PLAN / 03 STAGES</p><h2>One strong step<br /><span class="muted-heading">at a time.</span></h2></div></div><div class="roadmap-grid"><article class="roadmap-card roadmap-current"><span class="roadmap-index mono">PHASE 01 / NOW</span><span class="roadmap-icon">↗</span><h3>Web storefront</h3><p>Astro, TypeScript, responsive catalogue, dashboard previews, Cloudinary-ready image delivery, and Cloudflare Pages deployment.</p><span class="roadmap-status">IN PROGRESS</span></article><article class="roadmap-card"><span class="roadmap-index mono">PHASE 02 / NEXT</span><span class="roadmap-icon">⌘</span><h3>Secure backend</h3><p>Supabase Auth, PostgreSQL, role permissions, Row Level Security, trusted order functions, and real product data.</p><span class="roadmap-status">PLANNED</span></article><article class="roadmap-card"><span class="roadmap-index mono">PHASE 03 / LATER</span><span class="roadmap-icon">✳</span><h3>Multi-platform apps</h3><p>Kotlin Multiplatform with Compose Multiplatform for Android, iOS, and desktop where the platform requirements fit.</p><span class="roadmap-status">PLANNED</span></article></div></section>
  <section class="container principles-section"><div><p class="eyebrow">OUR PRINCIPLES</p><h2>Better foundations<br />make better <span class="coral-text">products.</span></h2></div><div class="principles-list"><div><span>01</span><p><strong>Security first</strong><br />No real customer data or sensitive actions in a public demo dashboard.</p></div><div><span>02</span><p><strong>Build in layers</strong><br />Keep the frontend, backend, and app clients clearly separated.</p></div><div><span>03</span><p><strong>Measure before scaling</strong><br />Start with a simple, understandable architecture and evolve when evidence requires it.</p></div><div><span>04</span><p><strong>Keep costs visible</strong><br />Prefer free tiers initially, monitor usage, and never enable paid services without approval.</p></div></div></section>
</SiteLayout>
